  "notes": [
    "Bulletin pages for BSc in Petroleum Geosciences and Remote Sensing (PGRS), Department of Applied Physics and Astronomy, College of Sciences. The program encompasses 123 credit hours over eight semesters (four years). Breakdown from the Program Overview table: University requirements 24 (15 compulsory + 9 elective), College requirements 15 compulsory, Program requirements 84 (50 mandatory core + 13 supportive + 15 elective + 6 general free elective); total 123.",
    "Semesters are printed 'Year n, Semester 1-8'; fall/spring is not stated, so 'semester' is null and 'term' holds the printed semester number.",
    "Course numbering: 7 digits (college no., dept. no., course level, specialized field, serial); specialized-field digit 1 = Petroleum, 2 = Geology, 3 = Remote Sensing, 0 = General (seminar, training, project).",
    "The plan tables do not label courses compulsory/elective; type is set only for courses listed in the 'Mandatory Core Courses' and 'Supportive Core Courses' tables (compulsory) and for elective slots (elective). Mandatory Core is stated as 50 credit hours but only 15 credit hours (five courses) are listed in the PDF.",
    "Rows with year null are the 13 'Elective Courses' (15 credit hours to be chosen) from the program bulletin; they are not placed in a semester. Elective slots keep placeholder codes 1460xxx as printed. The catalogue lists 1460226 Environmental Geology and Risk Management and 1460326 Advanced GIS, while the course-description pages print them as 1460325 and 1460426; codes are kept as in the elective table.",
    "Prerequisite inconsistencies in the plan tables (Year 1, Semester 2): Physics II is printed with prerequisite '1430117 (P/Co)' (its own code) and Physics II Lab with '1430118(P/Co), 1430211(P/Co)'. The Supportive Core table prints 1440131 (P/Co) and 1430110 for Physics II and 1430116 and 1430117 (P/Co) for Physics II Lab; the supportive-core values are used here. Training (1460400) prerequisite is printed '146311 & 65 credit hours completed' (146311 is probably 1460311); kept as printed. P/Co = prerequisite or co-requisite.",
    "Training (1460400) is described as eight weeks of internship in industry. Arabic Language is printed with two codes: 0201102, or 0201105 for non-Arabic speakers. Blank prerequisite cells are null."
  ]
}